{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107871","id":2610130991,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6bk3Av","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107871","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107871.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107871.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107871","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107871/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107871/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107871/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/678f12ee780b5be90d7e0cb093b224918c8a1192","number":107871,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Provide 'received headers' parameter for websocket server","user":{"login":"Portponky","id":33663279,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjYzMjc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33663279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Portponky","html_url":"https://github.com/Portponky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Portponky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Portponky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Portponky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Portponky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Portponky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Portponky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Portponky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Portponky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Portponky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is a small change that allows http and websockets to be provided through one endpoint.\r\n\r\nFor example, if you run a tcp server acting as an http endpoint providing two paths:\r\n\r\n/index.html -> serves a file through http get\r\n/ws -> opens a websocket connection\r\n\r\nAt the moment this is not really possible, because you need to read the incoming headers from the tcp stream to find out what the connection is trying to get. However, turning a StreamPeer into a websocket server through `accept_stream` requires that the full http header is sitting in the stream peer. Once you get the bytes out of the stream to examine them, you can no longer use `accept_stream` to let the connection act as a websocket server.\r\n\r\nThis change allows the received headers to be fed into accept_stream, which are then used to populate the handshake buffer. So, if you have already pulled out the first line, or the entire header, you can supply it when upgrading the connection to a websocket and it will use that.\r\n\r\nThe code to complete the handshake buffer was rearranged to first check f the buffer is complete, before reading from the connection to fill it.\r\n\r\nI have used this change in my game, to reduce it from requiring two separate endpoints (one for http and a separate one for websockets), to only one unified endpoint.\r\n\r\n- *Production edit: This closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12756.*","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":649800701,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NDk4MDA3MDE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:network","name":"topic:network","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/mil